class:: Pitch2
summary:: General modern F0 facade with explicit octave ambiguity
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Pitch, Classes/PitchYIN, Classes/PitchMPM

description::
Provides one entry point to MIR2's YIN and McLeod pitch engines. It returns frequency, algorithm-specific confidence, binary voicing, and competition from octave-related candidates instead of collapsing all evidence into one frequency. Octave ambiguity is code::competitor / (selected + competitor)::, where the competitor is the strongest local candidate near one-quarter, one-half, two, or four times the selected frequency within 80 cents.

For code::\yin::, confidence is one minus CMNDF; for code::\mpm::, it is NSDF clarity. Neither is a calibrated probability. A negative code::threshold:: selects the method default: 0.1 for YIN and 0.93 for MPM. Silence returns zero evidence and frequency unless code::hold:: is explicitly nonzero; while holding, confidence and voicing still fall to zero.

Frame scheduling and effective minimum frequency follow link::Classes/PitchYIN::. It is practically similar to link::Classes/Pitch::, but uses modern selectable paper-based algorithms, has explicit frame/hop semantics, exposes uncertainty, and does not silently hold stale pitch by default.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal. Multichannel expansion creates independent analyzers.

argument:: minFreq
Requested minimum F0 in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Maximum F0 in Hz, below Nyquist.

argument:: frameSize
Literal power-of-two frame size from 256 through 8192.

argument:: hop
Update hop as a frame fraction from 0.0625 through 1.

argument:: algorithm
Literal code::\yin::, code::\mpm::, or code::\swipe::. SWIPE dispatches to PitchSWIPE; use frameSize 8192 when the lower range needs about eight periods per window.

argument:: threshold
Negative uses the method default. Otherwise this is YIN CMNDF threshold or MPM peak cutoff.

argument:: smooth
Positive frequency smoothing time in seconds, performed in log-frequency space; 0 disables smoothing.

argument:: hold
Nonzero retains the last valid frequency during unvoiced frames without retaining confidence or voicing.

returns::
An Array: frequency in Hz, confidence from 0 through 1, voiced flag, and octave ambiguity from 0 through 1.

method:: latency
Returns approximate first-result latency in seconds.

instancemethods::

examples::
A tracked sine voice follows the source. Octave ambiguity attenuates the added voice when the evidence is uncertain.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var result = Pitch2.kr(source, 60, 2000, 2048, 0.25, \mpm);
        var tone = SinOsc.ar(result[0].clip(40, 2000).lag(0.03), 0, 0.07);
        ((source * 0.12) + (tone * result[2].lag(0.02) * (1 - (result[3] * 0.75)))) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.3) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

